<h2>What the terms and conditions say about buying tickets</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Who we are:</strong> Seat Outlet is an online marketplace for tickets to live events run by third parties such as venues, promoters, artists and sports teams.</li>
<li><strong>Prices and fees:</strong> ticket prices and any fees, taxes or charges are shown during the purchase process, and you agree to pay the total at checkout. They can change before purchase confirmation.</li>
<li><strong>Order acceptance:</strong> an order is accepted only when it is confirmed, for example by a confirmation email or by tickets being issued.</li>
<li><strong>Refunds:</strong> unless the terms, the event terms or the law say otherwise, ticket sales are final. Some events or promotions may offer different options, which are disclosed at purchase.</li>
<li><strong>Cancellations:</strong> if an event is canceled, postponed or materially changed, the organizer or venue usually decides whether you get a refund, a credit or a replacement ticket.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Your responsibilities under the terms and conditions</h2>
<ul>
<li>Under the terms and conditions, give accurate account and contact details and keep your login credentials confidential.</li>
<li>Meet venue entry rules, such as ID checks, age limits and security screening.</li>
<li>Use tickets for personal use unless resale is allowed on the platform or by the organizer.</li>
<li>Do not use bots, spiders or scrapers, including for bulk ticket purchasing.</li>
<li>Do not tamper with, forge or use tickets that are canceled, voided or reported lost or stolen.</li>
</ul>
<div class="so-callout"><p>The terms also say that Seat Outlet may suspend or terminate access, or cancel orders or tickets, if it reasonably believes the terms, the law or third-party rights have been violated. Read sections 10 and 18 above for the full wording.</p></div>

